WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.200
While the critics haven't been too kind to
The Rise of Skywalker, audience response has

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.480
been largely positive.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.660
So how did the cast of the film react to the
trilogy-ender?

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.140
Here's how the stars of Skywalker felt about
the final product.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:18.240
Speaking to Entertainment Tonight, Daisy Ridley
shared that it's unpleasant to read unfavorable

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:23.279
reviews, but a comment in one review stuck
with her: The Rise of Skywalker is a movie

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.040
for the fans.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.279
She told the magazine,

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:30.310
"The reason we collectively have made nine
[Star Wars films] is because people have loved

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.820
this for 42 years.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.160
That has to have been the driving force.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.000
A lot of people are hopefully going to see
it and a lot of people are hopefully going

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.600
to love it."

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.900
"Hey, I'm fun and I'm cool, come along on
this ride with me."

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.140
Ridley watched The Rise of Skywalker for the
first time with the rest of the cast early

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.480
in December, and admitted that she was so
overwhelmed she held her sister's hand throughout

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.580
the entire thing.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.400
At one point, Ridley wanted to leave the theater
to compose herself, preferring not to start

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.920
crying in front of people.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.340
She also shared that her other seat-mate was
pumped throughout the entire screening.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.500
Who might that have been?

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.340
None other than John Boyega, the actor behind
ex-stormtrooper-turned-Resistance-fighter

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.040
Finn.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.160
According to Ridley, Boyega did plenty of
whooping and cheering, with even a little

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.780
sideline commentary, for the duration of the
film.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:22.119
Oscar Isaac said that the first time he watched
the full theatrical cut of The Rise of Skywalker,

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:27.620
he, quote, "snot-cried," and was hoping to
shed only "manly tears" during the premiere.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:32.299
Isaac was also left with a lump in his throat
over the realization that with The Rise of

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:36.960
Skywalker, the Star Wars sequel trilogy is
complete, and that he'd be saying goodbye

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.420
to actors he's spent so many years working
with.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:44.940
The first online reaction to The Rise of Skywalker
from one of its cast members came from Richard

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.920
E. Grant, who plays General Pryde in the film.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.680
He took to Twitter after the cast first watched
the theatrical cut on December 4, posting

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.300
an emotional video about the completed project.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.560
Grant says he cheered, shouted, and even "fist-pumped
the air."

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:06.080
"It's absolutely everything that you hoped
it was going to be.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.480
I'm so proud to be in it."

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.680
Joonas Suotamo, who plays Chewbacca in the
Star Wars sequel trilogy, also took to his

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.459
Twitter account to react to The Rise of Skywalker,
thanking director J.J. Abrams for allowing

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:20.349
the cast an early screening of the film.

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:24.720
He also praised his fellow cast mates and
the crew behind the film, writing,

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.460
"Saw The Rise of Skywalker last night with
the cast.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.680
It was everything I'd hoped for and more!"

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.440
Other stars have been quieter about their
reactions to The Rise of Skywalker, perhaps

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.019
in an attempt to avoid letting any spoilers
slip before every Star Wars fan around the

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.420
world has had an opportunity to see the movie.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:46.960
Aside from sharing that he held hands with
Naomi Ackie during parts of the Rise of Skywalker

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:52.190
screening, John Boyega opted to close the
lid on further opinions to let the fans absorb

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.700
the film for themselves first.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.700
Ackie, who plays Jannah, said the vibe in
the theater during her Rise of Skywalker showing

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.140
was that of a celebration, with plenty of
cheering going on, particularly for the new

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:03.880
characters.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.420
Still, it took Ackie a while to process the
film for herself.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.840
She told Digital Spy,

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.460
"I didn't feel anything the first time I watched
it and I had to sleep on it.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:16.280
I just had to absorb it and figure out how
I felt slowly.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.220
The second time I watched it, it was like
a ride I loved it even more than the first

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:20.960
time.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.120
So the third time, who knows what will happen?

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.540
I've seen myself in the movie twice and it
still hasn't sunk in.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.940
It feels like I'm watching a completely different
person."

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:35.260
Anthony Daniels, who has been in each and
every one of the nine Skywalker saga installments,

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.540
is potentially saying goodbye to his character
with the new movie.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:44.300
He's played the beloved droid C-3PO for 42
years, since the very first Star Wars movie

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:49.739
from 1977, but recently admitted he would
probably be retiring from the character after

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.080
The Rise of Skywalker.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:55.540
It's a particularly emotional time for Daniels,
who admitted he needed a drink in his hand

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.660
when watching the film.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:00.700
"Sometimes I just don't understand human behavior."

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:06.220
For Adam Driver, there's a certain ambiguity
in The Rise of Skywalker that he really enjoys.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:11.480
With it being the final film not only of the
current trilogy but also of the whole nine-film

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.280
Skywalker saga, there's plenty of expectations
hanging over the movie.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.660
While this final chapter doesn't directly
answer all the burning questions fans may

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.010
have, Driver feels that The Rise of Skywalker
leaves audiences with a chance to fill in

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.260
the blanks for themselves.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.000
The actor told Cinema Blend,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.720
"It's for an audience to project their own
meaning towards.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.900
And luckily we had a script that honors ambiguity.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:37.940
[Chris Terrio) and J.J. Abrams] wrote something
that is not always spelled out in the dialogue,

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:38.680
which I love.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.980
It's not characters saying exactly what they're
feeling.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.380
it's a testament to, or keeps in the tradition
of the original movies.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.980
They're filled with so much ambiguity and
moments that I guess literally don't make

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:54.340
sense, but there's an emotional truth about
them that makes an audience project meaning."

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:59.160
Unlike what his character Kylo Ren is prone
to do, Driver kept his emotions at bay when

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.120
discussing the final installment of his Star
Wars career.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:07.160
And that's probably a wise choice, as it leaves
fans guessing his character's personal trajectory

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.160
and ultimate fate.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:12.720
Mark Hamill, who first had fans falling in
love with Star Wars back in the '70s when

00:05:12.721 --> 00:05:17.390
he stepped onto the screen as wide-eyed hero
Luke Skywalker, took to Instagram to thank

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:21.820
George Lucas for creating the galaxy far,
far away in the first place and for changing

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.120
his life in the process.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:28.571
"As #TheRiseOfSykwalker arrives in theaters,
let's not forget that it all started in the

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.620
imagination of just 1 man: GEORGE LUCAS.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:36.100
He alone created that galaxy far, far away
that has inspired generations.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.500
Then, he let me be a part of it &amp; changed
my life forever."

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:45.380
In true Hamill fashion, the actor also reminded
fans that spoilers are just plain uncool,

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.340
using the hashtag "MayTheShushBeWithYou" in
a separate post.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:53.620
Fans can form their own opinions on the flick
whenever they can get their butts in a theater

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.900
seat, as The Rise of Skywalker is finally
in theaters now.

